Consider the following XCal fragment:

@verbatim
<x:vevent xmlns:x="urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:icalendar-2.0">
  <x:properties>
    <x:dtstart>
      <x:parameters>
        <x:tzid><x:text>Europe/Stockholm</x:text></x:tzid>
      </x:parameters>
      <x:date-time>2025-09-07T12:41:48Z</x:date-time>
    </x:dtstart>
    <x:summary>
      <x:text>Hello</x:text>
    </x:summary>
  </x:properties>
</x:vevent>
@end verbatim

The top level @code{vevent} is a VComponent object of type
@code{'VEVENT}, with the @emph{properties} @code{dtstart} and @code{summary}.

The property @code{dtstart} in turn has one @emph{parameter}: @code{tzid}.

